---
---

<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<meta charset="utf-8" />
		<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
		<title>Game Master Guide - Untamed</title>
		<meta name="description" content="Run the hunt. The Untamed GM guide: hunt loop, monster AI, biomes, environmental systems, crafting, and quick references for the table." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<nav class="nav">
			<div class="container">
				<a href="/" class="logo">UNTAMED</a>
				<div class="nav-links">
					<a href="/rules">Rules</a>
					<a href="/quick-reference">Quick Reference</a>
					<a href="/character">Characters</a>
					<a href="/bestiary">Bestiary</a>
					<a href="/gm-guide" class="active">GM Guide</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</nav>

		<main>
			<!-- Hero / Welcome to the Wild -->
			<header class="hero">
				<div class="container">
					<p class="eyebrow">Game Master Guide</p>
					<h1>Welcome to the Wild</h1>
					<p class="lead">
						In Untamed, the world breathes through you. Every rustle in the underbrush, every storm that rolls across the valley,
						every roar in the distance — all of it begins with your voice and your choices. You are not a narrator in a static tale;
						you are the pulse of a living ecosystem that grows, fights back, and remembers.
					</p>
					<p class="lead">
						Your goal is simple: guide your hunters through a world that is both beautiful and brutal.
						Challenge them to think, to prepare, and to adapt — and reward their cleverness, not just their courage.
					</p>
				</div>
			</header>

			<!-- Your Role in the Wild -->
			<section class="role">
				<div class="container">
					<h2>Your Role in the Wild</h2>
					<div class="role-grid">
						<div class="role-card">
							<span class="icon">🌲</span>
							<h3>Embody the Living World</h3>
							<p>
								Nothing in Untamed stands still. The land shifts with the weather, monsters migrate when threatened,
								and even the smallest choice can ripple through the ecosystem. Portray that motion. Let the players feel
								that the world moves whether they act or not.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="role-card">
							<span class="icon">⚔️</span>
							<h3>Challenge Through Tactics</h3>
							<p>
								Every encounter should test endurance and wit. Victory is never guaranteed — it must be earned through
								timing, stamina, and understanding the creature's behavior. Force players to read the hunt, not just roll dice.
							</p>
						</div>
						<div class="role-card">
							<span class="icon">🩸</span>
							<h3>Reflect Choices Dynamically</h3>
							<p>
								The wild remembers. If the hunters burn a grove, the next hunt may begin in ash. If they spare a beast,
								it may return changed — as a rival, or as a myth. Every decision reshapes the balance of the world.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>

					<div class="creed">
						<p>This is not a tale of heroes saving kingdoms. It is a struggle for balance — hunters surviving the untamed wilds.</p>
						<p>A reckless blade is a broken blade. The wild does not forgive. But it rewards those who respect the hunt.</p>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Phases at a Glance -->
			<section class="phases">
				<div class="container">
					<h2>The Hunt Loop at a Glance</h2>
					<p class="section-lead">
						Four phases, porous on purpose. Weather, wounds, and monster behavior can kick you forward or backward.
						Your job is to keep the rhythm taut and the stakes real.
					</p>
					<div class="phase-grid">
						<div class="phase-card">
							<span class="phase-num">1</span>
							<h3>Gathering</h3>
							<p class="phase-tag">Research · Scout · Stock Up</p>
							<p>Collect rumors, identify monster traits, secure provisions, craft or upgrade gear. Spend stamina on travel and preparation.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="phase-card">
							<span class="phase-num">2</span>
							<h3>Tracking</h3>
							<p class="phase-tag">Find It Before It Finds You</p>
							<p>Follow tracks, analyze signs, avoid weather hazards. Perception and Instinct checks keep the trail alive.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="phase-card">
							<span class="phase-num">3</span>
							<h3>Combat</h3>
							<p class="phase-tag">Stamina · Timing · Terrain</p>
							<p>Manage stamina, exploit part breaks and conditions. Positioning matters. Don't forget defensive reactions and preparation actions.</p>
						</div>
						<div class="phase-card">
							<span class="phase-num">4</span>
							<h3>Resolution</h3>
							<p class="phase-tag">Harvest &amp; Fallout</p>
							<p>Deliver the final blow, harvest parts, resolve conditions, narrate consequences. Adjust the biome with territory shifts.</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Chapter Hub -->
			<section class="chapters">
				<div class="container">
					<h2>GM Guide Chapters</h2>
					<p class="section-lead">
						The book is big. Use this hub to jump to whatever you need at the table.
					</p>

					<div class="chapter-grid">
						<a href="/gm-guide/hunt-loop" class="chapter-card coming-soon">
							<span class="icon">🔁</span>
							<h3>The Hunt Loop</h3>
							<p class="description">Full phase-by-phase guidance: Gathering, Tracking, Combat, Resolution — with GM moves, typical rolls, and exit conditions.</p>
							<span class="label">Coming Soon</span>
						</a>

						<a href="/gm-guide/toolkit" class="chapter-card coming-soon">
							<span class="icon">🧰</span>
							<h3>GM Toolkit</h3>
							<p class="description">DC ranges, action economy, stamina cues, defensive reactions, save categories, and called shot adjudication.</p>
							<span class="label">Coming Soon</span>
						</a>

						<a href="/gm-guide/environment" class="chapter-card coming-soon">
							<span class="icon">🌦️</span>
							<h3>Environmental Systems</h3>
							<p class="description">Day/night cycle, camping &amp; rest, weather hazards, food &amp; cooking buffs, hydration, traversal, and night hunts.</p>
							<span class="label">Coming Soon</span>
						</a>

						<a href="/gm-guide/biomes" class="chapter-card coming-soon">
							<span class="icon">🗺️</span>
							<h3>Building &amp; Using Biomes</h3>
							<p class="description">Sector maps, ecology shifts, monster migrations, random events, villages, and a homebrew biome checklist.</p>
							<span class="label">Coming Soon</span>
						</a>

						<a href="/gm-guide/monsters" class="chapter-card coming-soon">
							<span class="icon">🐾</span>
							<h3>Monsters in Motion</h3>
							<p class="description">Behavior archetypes, instinct loops, classifications, the monster turn flow, tiers, thresholds, and small-monster handling.</p>
							<span class="label">Coming Soon</span>
						</a>

						<a href="/gm-guide/crafting" class="chapter-card coming-soon">
							<span class="icon">⚒️</span>
							<h3>Crafting &amp; Economy</h3>
							<p class="description">Material tags, monster effect tables, signature sets, traps, potions &amp; salves, and how the world's economy responds to the hunt.</p>
							<span class="label">Coming Soon</span>
						</a>

						<a href="/gm-guide/hunt-templates" class="chapter-card coming-soon">
							<span class="icon">🎯</span>
							<h3>Hunt Templates</h3>
							<p class="description">Alternative mission types: Track &amp; Slay, Harvest, Relocate, Rescue, Population Control, Ecology Disruption, Bait &amp; Observe.</p>
							<span class="label">Coming Soon</span>
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- Principle Tags -->
			<section class="tags">
				<div class="container">
					<h2>GM Principles vs. Rules</h2>
					<p class="section-lead">
						Throughout this guide you'll see labels that signal the intent of each paragraph. When in doubt, err on the side of player clarity and fun.
					</p>
					<ul class="tag-list">
						<li>
							<span class="tag hard">[Hard Rule]</span>
							A strict mechanic or requirement you should enforce. <em>"A hunter can perform only one preparation action per round."</em>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="tag soft">[Soft Rule]</span>
							A recommended guideline that can bend to context. <em>"Use exhaustion penalties sparingly."</em>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="tag guideline">[GM Guideline]</span>
							Advice for adjudicating situations. <em>"Telegraph monster attacks clearly."</em>
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="tag cue">[Narrative Cue]</span>
							Flavor text or prompts to inspire description; no mechanics attached.
						</li>
						<li>
							<span class="tag optional">[Optional Module]</span>
							Additional systems that can be toggled on or off (meal synergy, advanced pack behavior, etc.).
						</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>

			<footer class="footer">
				<div class="container">
					<p>
						This is the Playtest version. Some monster art is AI-generated; the final version will use original artist drawings.
					</p>
					<p class="footer-creed">The wild does not forgive. But it rewards those who respect the hunt.</p>
				</div>
			</footer>
		</main>

		<style>
			* {
				margin: 0;
				padding: 0;
				box-sizing: border-box;
			}

			:root {
				--forest-dark: #1a2e1a;
				--forest-green: #2d5016;
				--moss-green: #4a7c2f;
				--leaf-green: #6b9d3a;
				--amber: #d4a257;
				--earth-brown: #5c4033;
				--cream: #f5f1e8;
				--text-light: #e8e4d8;
			}

			body {
				font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, sans-serif;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				color: var(--text-light);
				line-height: 1.7;
				min-height: 100vh;
			}

			.container {
				max-width: 1200px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				padding: 0 2rem;
			}

			/* Navigation */
			.nav {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				border-bottom: 2px solid var(--amber);
				padding: 1rem 0;
				position: sticky;
				top: 0;
				z-index: 100;
			}

			.nav .container {
				display: flex;
				justify-content: space-between;
				align-items: center;
			}

			.logo {
				font-size: 1.5rem;
				font-weight: 900;
				color: var(--amber);
				text-decoration: none;
				letter-spacing: 0.2rem;
			}

			.nav-links {
				display: flex;
				gap: 2rem;
			}

			.nav-links a {
				color: var(--cream);
				text-decoration: none;
				font-weight: 500;
				transition: color 0.3s;
			}

			.nav-links a:hover,
			.nav-links a.active {
				color: var(--amber);
			}

			/* Hero */
			.hero {
				padding: 5rem 0 4rem;
				text-align: center;
				background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--forest-dark) 0%, var(--forest-green) 100%);
				border-bottom: 3px solid var(--amber);
			}

			.eyebrow {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				text-transform: uppercase;
				letter-spacing: 0.3rem;
				font-size: 0.95rem;
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
			}

			.hero h1 {
				font-size: 4rem;
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
				letter-spacing: 0.1rem;
				text-shadow: 2px 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
			}

			.lead {
				max-width: 820px;
				margin: 0 auto 1.25rem;
				font-size: 1.15rem;
				color: var(--cream);
			}

			/* Role Section */
			.role {
				padding: 5rem 0;
				background: var(--forest-green);
			}

			.role h2,
			.phases h2,
			.chapters h2,
			.tags h2 {
				text-align: center;
				font-size: 2.5rem;
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
			}

			.section-lead {
				text-align: center;
				max-width: 720px;
				margin: 0 auto 3rem;
				color: var(--cream);
				font-size: 1.05rem;
			}

			.role h2 {
				margin-bottom: 3rem;
			}

			.role-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr));
				gap: 2rem;
			}

			.role-card {
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				padding: 2rem;
				border-radius: 12px;
				border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown);
				transition: all 0.3s ease;
			}

			.role-card:hover {
				border-color: var(--amber);
				transform: translateY(-4px);
			}

			.role-card .icon {
				font-size: 2.5rem;
				display: block;
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
			}

			.role-card h3 {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
				font-size: 1.35rem;
			}

			.creed {
				margin-top: 3rem;
				padding: 2rem;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);
				border-radius: 6px;
				text-align: center;
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--cream);
			}

			.creed p + p {
				margin-top: 0.75rem;
			}

			/* Phases */
			.phases {
				padding: 5rem 0;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
			}

			.phase-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr));
				gap: 1.5rem;
			}

			.phase-card {
				background: var(--forest-green);
				padding: 2rem;
				border-radius: 12px;
				border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown);
				position: relative;
				transition: all 0.3s ease;
			}

			.phase-card:hover {
				border-color: var(--amber);
				transform: translateY(-4px);
			}

			.phase-num {
				position: absolute;
				top: -1rem;
				right: 1.5rem;
				font-size: 3.5rem;
				font-weight: 900;
				color: var(--amber);
				opacity: 0.4;
				line-height: 1;
			}

			.phase-card h3 {
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
				font-size: 1.5rem;
			}

			.phase-tag {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				text-transform: uppercase;
				letter-spacing: 0.1rem;
				font-size: 0.8rem;
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
			}

			/* Chapter Hub */
			.chapters {
				padding: 5rem 0;
				background: var(--forest-green);
			}

			.chapter-grid {
				display: grid;
				grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(320px, 1fr));
				gap: 2rem;
			}

			.chapter-card {
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				padding: 2rem;
				border-radius: 12px;
				border: 2px solid var(--earth-brown);
				transition: all 0.3s ease;
				text-decoration: none;
				color: inherit;
				display: block;
			}

			.chapter-card:not(.coming-soon):hover {
				border-color: var(--amber);
				transform: translateY(-4px);
				box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(212, 162, 87, 0.3);
			}

			.chapter-card.coming-soon {
				opacity: 0.65;
				cursor: not-allowed;
			}

			.chapter-card .icon {
				font-size: 3rem;
				display: block;
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
			}

			.chapter-card h3 {
				color: var(--amber);
				margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
				font-size: 1.5rem;
			}

			.description {
				color: var(--text-light);
				margin-bottom: 1rem;
				font-size: 1rem;
			}

			.label {
				display: inline-block;
				padding: 0.25rem 0.75rem;
				background: var(--amber);
				color: var(--forest-dark);
				border-radius: 4px;
				font-size: 0.85rem;
				font-weight: 600;
				text-transform: uppercase;
				letter-spacing: 0.05rem;
			}

			.coming-soon .label {
				background: var(--earth-brown);
				color: var(--cream);
			}

			/* Tags Section */
			.tags {
				padding: 5rem 0;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
			}

			.tag-list {
				list-style: none;
				max-width: 800px;
				margin: 0 auto;
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				gap: 1rem;
			}

			.tag-list li {
				padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
				background: var(--forest-green);
				border-left: 4px solid var(--earth-brown);
				border-radius: 6px;
				color: var(--text-light);
			}

			.tag-list em {
				color: var(--leaf-green);
			}

			.tag {
				display: inline-block;
				font-weight: 700;
				font-size: 0.85rem;
				margin-right: 0.75rem;
				padding: 0.15rem 0.5rem;
				border-radius: 3px;
				color: var(--forest-dark);
				white-space: nowrap;
			}

			.tag.hard {
				background: #d97757;
			}

			.tag.soft {
				background: var(--amber);
			}

			.tag.guideline {
				background: var(--leaf-green);
			}

			.tag.cue {
				background: #a888c4;
			}

			.tag.optional {
				background: var(--cream);
			}

			/* Footer */
			.footer {
				padding: 3rem 0;
				background: var(--forest-dark);
				border-top: 3px solid var(--earth-brown);
				text-align: center;
				color: var(--moss-green);
			}

			.footer p {
				font-size: 0.95rem;
				margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
			}

			.footer-creed {
				font-style: italic;
				color: var(--leaf-green);
				margin-top: 1rem;
			}

			/* Responsive */
			@media (max-width: 768px) {
				.nav .container {
					flex-direction: column;
					gap: 1rem;
				}

				.nav-links {
					gap: 1rem;
					flex-wrap: wrap;
					justify-content: center;
				}

				.hero h1 {
					font-size: 2.5rem;
				}

				.role h2,
				.phases h2,
				.chapters h2,
				.tags h2 {
					font-size: 2rem;
				}

				.chapter-grid,
				.role-grid {
					grid-template-columns: 1fr;
				}
			}
		</style>
	</body>
</html>
